From: Jim Huang <jserv@ccns.ncku.edu.tw>
Subject: [PATCH] tiny: arm: add UNWINDER_NONE option

Introduce a third entry in the ARM "Choose kernel unwinder" choice that
selects neither CONFIG_ARM_UNWIND nor CONFIG_FRAME_POINTER. On size-
constrained Cortex-M targets the EABI unwind tables (.ARM.exidx /
.ARM.extab) account for tens of KB of otherwise-dead metadata: the only
runtime consumer is panic-time backtrace formatting, which a serial-
only board can do without.

UNWINDER_FRAME_POINTER cannot be selected on THUMB2_KERNEL because the
existing frame-pointer unwinder assumes ARM-mode prologues, and
UNWINDER_ARM forces ARM_UNWIND=y, so a no-op option is required to let
arch/arm/kernel/vmlinux.lds.S DISCARD the unwind sections.

Provide a tiny stub unwind_frame() that returns -EINVAL when neither
ARM_UNWIND nor FRAME_POINTER is configured. __get_wchan() and
walk_stackframe() therefore still link, but produce a single-frame
trace instead of a full call chain.

CAVEAT: arch_stack_walk() (compiled only when CONFIG_STACKTRACE=y) does
a pre-skip "if (unwind_frame(&frame)) return;" before calling
walk_stackframe(), so under UNWINDER_NONE that path returns ZERO frames
instead of one. Harmless while STACKTRACE remains off; if a future
build enables STACKTRACE=y, switch back to UNWINDER_ARM or extend the
stub to advance once for the synthetic skip frame.

---
 arch/arm/Kconfig             | 2 +-
 arch/arm/Kconfig.debug       | 7 +++++++
 arch/arm/kernel/stacktrace.c | 7 +++++++
 3 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/Kconfig b/arch/arm/Kconfig
--- a/arch/arm/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/Kconfig
@@ -1123,7 +1123,7 @@ config THUMB2_KERNEL
 	bool "Compile the kernel in Thumb-2 mode" if !CPU_THUMBONLY
 	depends on (CPU_V7 || CPU_V7M) && !CPU_V6 && !CPU_V6K
 	default y if CPU_THUMBONLY
-	select ARM_UNWIND
+	select ARM_UNWIND if !UNWINDER_NONE
 	help
 	  By enabling this option, the kernel will be compiled in
 	  Thumb-2 mode.

diff --git a/arch/arm/Kconfig.debug b/arch/arm/Kconfig.debug
--- a/arch/arm/Kconfig.debug
+++ b/arch/arm/Kconfig.debug
@@ -72,6 +72,13 @@ config UNWINDER_ARM
 	  compiler. The resulting kernel image is slightly bigger but
 	  the performance is not affected. Currently, this feature
 	  only works with EABI compilers.
+
+config UNWINDER_NONE
+	bool "No unwinder (smallest image)"
+	help
+	  Disable kernel-side stack unwinding. Panic and warning backtraces
+	  collapse to a single frame, but the EABI unwind tables
+	  (.ARM.exidx/.ARM.extab) are discarded, saving tens of KB.

 endchoice

diff --git a/arch/arm/kernel/stacktrace.c b/arch/arm/kernel/stacktrace.c
--- a/arch/arm/kernel/stacktrace.c
+++ b/arch/arm/kernel/stacktrace.c
@@ -123,6 +123,13 @@ int notrace unwind_frame(struct stackframe *frame)
 }
 #endif

+#if !defined(CONFIG_ARM_UNWIND) && !defined(CONFIG_FRAME_POINTER)
+int notrace unwind_frame(struct stackframe *frame)
+{
+	return -EINVAL;
+}
+#endif
+
 void notrace walk_stackframe(struct stackframe *frame,
 		     bool (*fn)(void *, unsigned long), void *data)
 {
